# Coreside Project Context

## Product Identity

The product is named:

Coreside

Always use exactly this capitalization.

Do not use:

- CoreSide
- Core Side
- Core-Side
- Coreside AI as the primary product name
- Partial Update as the product name
- Provider-specific branding as the product identity
- Temporary scaffold names

Coreside is a consumer-first, AI-native desktop application in which the AI does not merely create external applications or files. The AI progressively builds, modifies, and expands the application environment that the user is already using.

The application begins as a capable conversational AI interface. Over time, each user’s version of Coreside becomes structurally different because the user can ask the agent to create personal tools, dashboards, interfaces, automations, wallpapers, settings, layouts, workflows, games, and other persistent capabilities inside Coreside itself.

Every installation begins from the same protected foundation, but the user-editable layer evolves differently for every person.

The central product idea is:

> Coreside is a conversational application that can progressively build itself around the user.

Coreside should not be treated as:

- A normal chatbot with a few generated widgets
- A generic app builder that only exports external websites
- An unrestricted code-generation sandbox
- An IDE
- A browser
- A collection of disconnected AI tools
- A marketplace-first product
- An enterprise dashboard
- A wrapper around one AI provider
- A clone of ChatGPT, Claude, or Partial Update

Its primary differentiation is that conversations can become persistent internal software.

