# AI Provider Architecture

Coreside must remain provider-neutral.

The application may support providers such as:

- Google Gemini
- OpenAI
- Anthropic
- OpenRouter
- Compatible providers added through trusted adapters

Do not make the product identity dependent on one model provider.

The user should be able to:

- Enter a provider key through a protected BYOK interface
- Store the key securely through the operating system
- Select an active provider
- Select a model
- Test the connection
- Replace the key
- Remove a provider
- Retain `.env` support as a development fallback

API keys must never be stored in:

- SQLite
- localStorage
- Generated tools
- Agent messages
- Action Logs
- Exports
- Search caches
- Diagnostics
- Plaintext application settings

Do not silently fall back from secure credential storage to plaintext.

