# Automations

Users may create safe recurring automations.

Examples:

- Rotate backgrounds every five hours
- Reset a tracker daily
- Clear completed tasks weekly
- Run a checklist every morning
- Change a tool setting at a scheduled time

Prefer deterministic automations.

Use AI-backed automations only when the result genuinely requires model generation.

AI-backed automations must disclose:

- Provider use
- Model use
- API-credit use
- Frequency
- Requirement that Coreside is running

Automations must be:

- Persisted
- Bounded
- Cancelable
- Pauseable
- Editable
- Deletable
- Protected against duplicate concurrent runs
- Protected against catch-up storms
- Protected against repeated failure loops

The scheduler belongs in trusted Rust infrastructure.

Do not allow arbitrary shell, Python, or JavaScript automations.

