# Persistence and Versioning

The defining value of Coreside depends on persistence.

A generated feature is not complete if it disappears after restart.

Persist where appropriate:

- Chats
- Projects
- Project membership
- Project instructions
- Summaries
- Tools
- Surfaces
- Surface state
- Component definitions
- Added Settings
- Wallpapers
- Automations
- Media
- Branches
- Snapshots
- Versions
- Application transactions
- Citations
- Approved layouts

Use automatic database migrations.

Existing user data must survive upgrades.

Persistent application changes should be versioned and undoable where practical.

Cross-surface changes should use transaction-level history so one undo can restore all resources changed by one approved agent action.

